%% SignFlow — IMPLEMENTED remote signing flow (verified against the code, Oct 2026)
%% Desktop: ui/, client/, token/, signing/, verification/   Server: server/** (profile "server")
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    box rgb(228,237,248) User's PC - local only
        participant D as SignFlow Desktop (JavaFX)
        participant P as PKCS#35;11 provider (SunPKCS11 + vendor DLL)
        participant C as USB token / smart card
    end
    box rgb(221,241,238) SignFlow server - Spring Boot
        participant S as REST controllers
        participant A as Spring Security (SecurityConfig, AuthenticatedRequestFilter) + GuestAccessPolicy
        participant W as RemoteWorkflowService
        participant I as InvitationService
        participant DB as PostgreSQL (JPA, Flyway V1-V6)
        participant F as DocumentFileStorage (PDF files on disk)
    end

    Note over D: Local start-up gate (LoginDialog): checks signature.login.* in config.<br/>It is NOT a server login.

    alt Account holder (sender or registered signer)
        U->>D: Username + password
        D->>S: POST /api/auth/login
        S->>DB: Check bcrypt hash (users)
        alt Wrong credentials
            S-->>D: 401
            D-->>U: "Incorrect username or password"
        else Valid
            S-->>D: Access JWT (15 min) + refresh token
            Note over D,S: Refresh: POST /api/auth/refresh with rotation and reuse detection
        end
    else Invited signer (no account)
        U->>D: Clicks email link /invitations/{token} then signflow://invitation/{token}
        Note over D: Only the token is read from the link.<br/>The server URL comes from local config.
        D->>S: GET /api/invitations/{token} (preview)
        S->>I: Look up SHA-256(token), check status and expiry
        I->>DB: invitations, workflows
        D->>S: POST /api/invitations/{token}/guest-code
        alt Expired, revoked, replaced or already used by another slot
            S-->>D: 4xx (INVITATION_EXPIRED / REVOKED / ALREADY_USED)
            D-->>U: Error message, ask sender to resend
        else Valid
            I->>DB: Store SHA-256 of a one-time 6-digit code (10 min, 5 tries)
            I-->>U: E-mail the code to the invited address only
            U->>D: Type the code
            D->>S: POST /api/invitations/{token}/guest-session (code)
            I->>DB: Check and consume the code, status ACCEPTED, audit SIGNING_SESSION_CREATED
            S-->>D: Guest JWT scoped to one workflow and one signer slot
        end
    end

    D->>S: GET /api/workflows/{id}/task (Bearer JWT)
    S->>A: Validate JWT (guest: GuestAccessPolicy allow-list)
    A->>W: Authorised user or guest
    W->>DB: Workflow, signer slots, current revision
    S-->>D: Task view (turn, policy, bound certificate, placement)
    D->>S: GET /api/workflows/{id}/document
    W->>F: Read current revision PDF
    S-->>D: PDF bytes
    D->>D: Load manifest + verify existing signatures locally (WorkflowSigningService)

    D->>P: TokenService.detect()
    P->>C: C_GetSlotList, C_GetTokenInfo, C_FindObjects (certificates, no PIN)
    alt No token / driver not loaded
        P-->>D: Exception
        D-->>U: Red status "Smart card driver problem / could not be read"
    else Token present
        C-->>D: Token info + certificates
        D->>D: SigningCardCheck: compare with fingerprint bound to this step
    end

    opt Slot still unbound (workflow in DRAFT)
        D->>S: POST /api/workflows/{id}/signers/{user}/certificate (SHA-256 fingerprint)
        W->>DB: Bind fingerprint. Last binding prepares revision 0
    end

    loop Until unlocked or user cancels
        U->>D: Enter PIN (char[] wiped after use)
        D->>P: AuthProvider.login (C_Login)
        alt Wrong PIN
            P-->>D: CKR_PIN_INCORRECT
            D-->>U: "Incorrect PIN", card locks after a few tries
        else PIN locked
            P-->>D: CKR_PIN_LOCKED
            D-->>U: "PIN locked", stop
        else OK
            P-->>D: Session authenticated
        end
    end

    U->>D: Place stamp, confirm in "Ready to Sign" checkpoint
    D->>D: PDFBox incremental revision + manifest. Build CMS signed attributes (SHA-256)
    D->>P: Signature SHA256withRSA (signed attributes)
    P->>C: C_Sign with on-card private key
    C-->>D: Signature bytes (private key never leaves the card)
    D->>D: Embed CMS (adbe.pkcs7.detached), re-open, verify whole chain
    alt Local verification fails
        D-->>U: "Signing failed: document not modified"
    end

    D->>S: POST /api/workflows/{id}/signatures (signed PDF, parentRevision, parentSha256, signingOperationId)
    S->>A: Validate JWT / guest scope
    A->>W: submitSignature
    alt Same signingOperationId already accepted
        W-->>D: Previous result (idempotent replay)
    else Not this user's turn
        W-->>D: 409 NOT_YOUR_TURN
    else Parent revision or hash is stale
        W-->>D: 409 revision conflict
    else Validation fails
        Note over W: Checks: pure incremental update of parent bytes, every signature valid,<br/>exactly parent+1 signatures, newest cert = bound fingerprint, no mock identity
        W->>DB: Audit SIGNATURE_VALIDATION_FAILED (status unchanged)
        W-->>D: 4xx (DOCUMENT_MODIFIED / INVALID_SIGNATURE / CERTIFICATE_MISMATCH)
    else Accepted
        W->>F: Write immutable revision N+1
        W->>DB: document_versions, signer signed, audit events
        W->>DB: SIGNATURE_SUBMITTED -> VALIDATING -> WAITING_FOR_SIGNER or COMPLETED
        S-->>D: Accepted as revision N+1 + new state
    end

    D-->>U: Success screen (view document, signature details, download signed PDF)
    opt Later
        U->>D: Open task again
        D->>S: GET /api/workflows/{id}/document and /revisions, /audit
        S-->>D: Final signed PDF + history
    end

    Note over S,DB: Not implemented: certificate trust/revocation (TrustStatus NOT_VERIFIED),<br/>timestamping, webhooks, partner API. Only the first invitation is emailed.
